old:
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "name": "Superflow vs Userback: Side-by-Side Comparison (August 2026)",
  "mainEntity": [
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Should my agency use Superflow or Userback for client review cycles?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "If your team manages web builds and needs AI to run QA automatically before clients approve live work, Superflow is the stronger fit. Userback is built for internal product and QA teams tracking bugs at scale, so the tool works best when your reviewers are developers and testers, not external clients."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How does Superflow's AI layer differ from Userback's feedback tools?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Superflow converts any QA checklist into named AI agents that run automatically on every site change, posting findings as pinned comments on the exact element. Built-in agents cover Accessibility, Broken Links, Spell Check, and OG Images; you can build custom agents for any checklist item. Memory makes agents smarter with every project by learning each client's rules and past decisions. Userback offers AI-assisted tagging to sort incoming feedback, but does not scan your site automatically, so your team still runs the first pass manually."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Who is Userback best suited for, and where does Superflow serve agencies better?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Userback fits product managers and developers who need structured bug capture from end users during testing cycles, with session replays and metadata baked in. Superflow is built for agencies delivering client work, where the priority is collecting feedback on live staging URLs, getting sign-offs without login friction, and keeping comments organized across mixed-media projects."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Can clients leave feedback in Superflow without creating an account?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes. Clients click a link, click anywhere on the live page, and leave a comment with no login or app install required. Userback uses an embedded widget for feedback collection, and external reporters can submit through it without creating an account. The more meaningful gap is that Userback has no dedicated approval workflow or sign-off link, there is no equivalent of sending a client a link to formally approve a deliverable. Sign-off typically happens outside the tool, over email or a separate channel, which adds steps and slows down the handoff."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What should I consider before switching from Userback to Superflow?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "If your current workflow depends on session replays or mobile app bug reporting, Userback covers those use cases and Superflow does not. Superflow is the right move if your bottleneck is client approval speed, mixed-asset review across websites, PDFs, video, images, and Lottie files, or running AI-powered QA checks automatically on every deploy without adding separate tooling to your stack."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How does Superflow's pricing compare to Userback's?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Superflow has a free Starter plan and paid plans starting at $24/seat/month (annual) or $29/seat/month (monthly). Guest seats are always free and unlimited, so clients reviewing and approving work never count against your seat total. Userback's paid plans start at $29/month, with feature access scaling steeply at higher tiers. For agencies managing multiple client projects, Superflow's unlimited free guest seats keep costs predictable as your client roster grows."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Which website builders and CMS platforms does Superflow support?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Superflow installs in one click on Webflow, WordPress, Framer, Shopify, Wix, Bubble, Drupal, Elementor, Squarespace, HubSpot, and Google Tag Manager. For any other site, a single script tag handles installation. AI agents go live the moment the snippet is in place, with no extra configuration needed to start running QA checks. Userback also uses a JavaScript snippet for installation with comparable CMS coverage for web apps."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Is Superflow SOC 2 or HIPAA compliant?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes. Superflow is SOC 2 Type II certified and HIPAA-compliant, with a BAA available. It also supports data residency, end-to-end encryption, SAML/SSO and SCIM (both on Enterprise), and keeps a full audit trail of every comment, finding, and approval. For agencies working with clients in healthcare, legal, or financial services, those compliance credentials remove a common procurement blocker that comes up before sign-off."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Does Superflow replace separate QA testing tools, or does it sit alongside them?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Superflow replaces the need for a separate QA tool in most agency workflows. AI agents run your checklist automatically on every site change, covering Accessibility, Broken Links, Spell Check, and OG Images, plus any custom checks you build, so there is no gap between your build step and client approval."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How does Superflow's Memory feature work across multiple client projects?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Memory is scoped per client, so rules, brand guides, and past decisions learned on one project carry into future projects for that client without bleeding into other accounts. By the time you reach project ten, agents already know what project one had to learn the hard way."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What types of files can I get client feedback on inside Superflow?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Superflow supports pinned comments on websites, PDFs, video, images, and Lottie files, all inside one project. That means a client can review a staging site, a PDF brand guide, and static mockups in a single feedback thread without you switching tools between asset types."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Does Userback support automated QA checks on staging sites before client review?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "No. Userback's AI layer categorizes and groups incoming feedback from human reporters, but it does not run automated scans on your site. Your team still performs the first QA pass manually before sending anything to a client, which adds time to every delivery cycle."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How do Superflow's AI agent credits work, and do unused credits roll over?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Each agent review costs 10 credits per page, and unused credits roll over monthly so you are not paying for capacity you did not use. The Starter plan includes 60 credits per month, Growth gives 300, Scale gives 600, and add-on packs start at 500 credits for $18."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Can I white-label the client review portal in Superflow?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes, white-label client portals are available on the Scale plan and above, letting you present the review experience under your agency brand. Userback does not offer a white-label option, which matters if brand consistency in client-facing tools is part of how your agency operates."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How do I install Superflow on a site built with Webflow, Framer, or a custom codebase?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Webflow, WordPress, Framer, and Shopify get a one-click install with no code required. For any other site, including custom codebases, a single script tag handles the whole setup. AI agents go live the moment the snippet is in place."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What project management tools sync with Superflow, and is the sync two-way?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Superflow syncs two ways with Jira, Asana, ClickUp, Monday.com, and Trello, so comments create tasks and sign-offs close them automatically. Slack notifications let you reply in-thread without switching tabs, and a connector going down never blocks a review because events queue and retry."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What is the fastest way for an agency to get AI-powered QA running on a client site?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Add the Superflow snippet or use the one-click install for Webflow, Framer, WordPress, or Shopify, then paste your QA checklist or upload a brand guide. Agents start checking on the next site change with no engineer required and no additional configuration needed."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "When does it make more sense to use Userback over Superflow?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Userback is the better fit if your team needs session replays, mobile app bug reporting from end users, or structured bug capture from internal testers during development cycles. Superflow is built for the agency delivery cycle where the goal is automated QA on every deploy followed by a fast, friction-free client sign-off."
      }
    }
  ],
  "url": "https://usesuperflow.ai/blog/superflow-vs-userback-website-feedback",
  "dateModified": "2026-08-12T23:13:49.576Z",
  "author": {
    "@type": "Organization",
    "name": "Superflow"
  }
}

