  "name": "Best Creative Approval Software Ranked (September 2026)",
  "mainEntity": [
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How do I choose between Superflow, Atarim, Filestage, Pastel, and Frame.io for my agency?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Start with your primary asset type and team size. Frame.io wins for video-only post-production teams inside Adobe Creative Cloud; Pastel works for freelancers who need fast visual feedback with zero setup; Filestage fits marketing teams running structured sign-off chains on creative files; Atarim suits WordPress maintenance agencies that want a white-labeled client portal; Superflow is the strongest fit for agencies delivering websites alongside mixed assets who need automated QA, per-client memory, and two-way PM sync."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Is Superflow better than Pastel for agencies that review live websites?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes, for agencies with more than a handful of active clients. Pastel lets clients comment on a URL without any account, which works well for simple feedback collection, but it has no AI layer, no automated QA, and no two-way task sync. Superflow runs QA agents on every deploy and carries client-specific rules forward project to project, so reviews start with findings already posted rather than a blank canvas."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "When should I choose Filestage over Superflow for creative approvals?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Choose Filestage when your work lives primarily in uploaded files, your team is deeply embedded in Adobe Premiere, Photoshop, or InDesign, and you need formal multi-step approval routing with reviewer groups and due dates. If your deliverables include live websites or you need HIPAA compliance, Filestage's gaps become blockers and Superflow covers both."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Can clients approve work in these tools without creating an account?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "It depends on the tool. Superflow and Pastel both let clients review and approve through a shared link with no login required. Filestage also supports guest reviewers without an account. Atarim routes client work through a branded portal that does require client access. Frame.io has limited guest options depending on the plan. If reducing client friction at sign-off is a priority, Superflow, Pastel, and Filestage are the cleaner options."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Which creative approval tools include SOC 2 Type II and HIPAA compliance?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Of the five tools in this list, only Superflow publicly documents both SOC 2 Type II and HIPAA with a BAA. Atarim holds SOC 2 Type II but does not publicly advertise HIPAA coverage. Frame.io offers SOC 2 on Enterprise plans. Filestage carries ISO 27001 rather than SOC 2. Pastel has no publicly documented compliance certifications. For agencies handling healthcare clients or any work requiring a formal BAA, Superflow is the only confirmed option here."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What's the fastest way to set up automated QA on a client site without involving a developer?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Add Superflow's snippet to any site, or use the one-click install for Webflow, WordPress, Framer, or Shopify — no engineer required. Once the snippet is in, you paste your checklist or upload a brand guide, and agents start checking on every deploy automatically."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Should I use Frame.io or Superflow when my agency delivers both video and website assets?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Use Superflow if your projects mix websites with video, PDF, images, and Lottie files, since Frame.io only handles video and has no live website review or automated QA. Frame.io is the right call only when video post-production inside Adobe Creative Cloud is the entire scope of the work."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How does per-client memory work in creative approval software?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Superflow's Memory stores each client's brand rules, past decisions, and learned preferences from every review, scoped so no rules carry over between clients. By the tenth project, agents already know what the first project had to catch manually, so QA starts more accurate than it finished last time."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What is deploy-triggered QA and why does it matter for web agencies?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Deploy-triggered QA means AI agents run checks automatically every time a site change goes live, without anyone on your team initiating the scan. For agencies shipping frequent updates, this closes the window between a change going out and a problem getting caught — rather than relying on someone remembering to kick off a review."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Can I build custom AI review agents for my agency's specific QA checklist?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes, in Superflow you can build custom agents for any checklist item through a prompt-and-test interface, on top of the built-in agents for accessibility, broken links, spell check, and OG images. Agents post findings as pinned comments on the exact element that triggered them, so the output is already contextualized when your team opens the project."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Which creative approval tools work best for freelancers vs. mid-size agencies?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Pastel suits freelancers who need fast, zero-setup visual feedback with no client onboarding friction, and it starts at $35/month. Mid-size agencies running multiple clients and asset types get more from Superflow, which adds automated QA, per-client memory, two-way PM sync, and compliance coverage that freelance-tier tools don't offer."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How do I keep client feedback organized across multiple projects without losing sign-off records?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Use a tool with version tracking, a full audit trail, and structured approval gates so every sign-off is recorded and searchable. Superflow logs every comment, finding, and approval, and preserves feedback across versions so you can point to exactly who approved what and when."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Do creative approval tools integrate with project management software like Asana or Jira?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Several do, but the depth varies. Superflow offers two-way sync with Asana, Monday.com, ClickUp, Trello, and Jira — comments create tasks, sign-offs close them, and statuses sync both ways. Filestage also integrates with those tools, and Pastel offers one-way export only on its Team plan."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What's the difference between a proxy-based website review tool and a snippet-based one?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "A proxy tool like Pastel renders a copy of your URL in its own canvas, requiring no install but giving you limited control over what the client sees and no ability to trigger automated checks on deploys. A snippet-based tool like Superflow runs directly on the live site, which lets AI agents check every real change automatically and post findings on the actual elements in context."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How should I evaluate creative approval software if my agency works with healthcare clients?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "HIPAA compliance with a signed BAA should be a hard filter, not a nice-to-have — without it, your agency takes on liability for any protected health information that passes through the review process. Of the tools in this comparison, Superflow is the only one that publicly documents HIPAA with BAA, starting at $24 per seat per month on an annual plan."
      }
    }
  ],
  "url": "https://usesuperflow.ai/blog/best-creative-approval-tools",
  "dateModified": "2026-09-27T18:20:32.416Z",
  "author": {
    "@type": "Organization",
    "name": "Superflow"
  }
}

